## Commands Used

| Command | Description |
|---|---|
| `nano exp7.c` | Creates the C program. |
| `gcc exp7.c -o exp7` | Compiles the C program. |
| `./exp7` | Executes the program. |
| `top` | Monitors CPU and process usage in real time. |
| `Ctrl + C` | Terminates the running program. |

## Observation

After executing the CPU-bound program, we observed that the CPU utilization increased significantly. The `top` command displayed the running process and its CPU usage.

The program continuously performs calculations inside an infinite loop, which keeps the CPU busy.

## Conclusion

In this experiment, we created a CPU-bound C program using an infinite loop that continuously performs calculations. We monitored its CPU utilization using the Linux `top` command. We observed that the program consumed a significant amount of CPU resources while running. This experiment helped us understand CPU-bound processes and CPU utilization in Linux.
